opencl: row broadcast of a src1 row that repeats along dim 0
Fold-into: upstream/ggml-opencl

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9 plus every patch of the series before this one.

ADD, SUB, MUL and DIV take the row kernels when src1 is one contiguous row with
ne10 % 4 == 0 and ne00 % 4 == 0. The kernels read src1 at the flat index gid
modulo ne, and the host set ne = ne00/4. When src1 repeats along dim 0
(ne10 < ne00), the index goes past the src1 row. The op fuzzer found relative
errors of 0.52 and 1.0, for example ADD of f16[32,12] and f16[16,1]. The app
graphs do not reach this condition: no ADD or MUL of their graphs repeats src1
along dim 0.

This patch sets ne = ne10/4. ggml_can_repeat makes ne00 a multiple of ne10,
thus the element of the flat index gid is gid % (ne10/4).

The patch also adds bin_bcast cases to test-backend-ops: f16 and f32 src1 rows
of 16 and 8 elements that repeat two times along dim 0.

